1. *Candidate's causal claim corrected:* the §9 pattern's "same author writes the claim and checks it" is **consistent with the evidence, not established by it** — Wave 34 establishes that builder readiness checks let deficient receipts reach jev-prewave on all five items; it does not establish shared authorship as the cause or independence as the cure. The candidate stands NOT-YET-AMENDED with consumer HQ, its owning surfaces named: INSTRUCTION.md §5 leg 3b (the readiness step) + the mechanical guard layer (guards.md). **Acceptance test for HQ, from the filed failures:** any landed form must catch, on the filed Wave-34 records, (a) T199's A-8 — the exact probe and window a receipt claims must exist in the filed raw output (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T199-shout-scaling-in-real-scene/codex/jev-prewave-completion2.md`, findings 1–2); (b) T199's B-17 — an observed swapped color must be printed by the swap receipt it is claimed under (same return); (c) T205's CP01 class — a binding predicate evaluated AT its endpoint (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, finding 1: `stateAt(570 ms)` = exactly 0.30 against a strict < 0.30 bound). A grep-for-instant + CONFIG-diff check alone would miss (b) and (c) — the test says so on its face. The handoff's board state: HQ.json still carries this wave's Plan skeleton at firing time; the closed entry (§10 filings) is the handoff's confirmation.
2. *Mechanical guards, complete disposition:* command 4 (scores arithmetic) — **NOT DEMANDED this cycle** (no lens scores exist to consolidate; its non-firing is the two-HOLD rule's consequence, not an omission). Commands 2/6/7 — their REQUIREMENTS are sound; three FILED OUTPUTS were deficient, which supports deferring a receipt-validation change to HQ rather than amending guard text here: command 2 (swap) — T208's re-fire found no regenerated-geometry result under content swap (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T208-paired-dot-counts-house-stage/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`) AND T210's re-fire names command-2 output defects of its own: a stale swap instant in its index and palette swap without observed output values (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T210-threshold-grid-map/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`) · command 6 (fit leg) — T204's swap-title fit row lacked a measured post-fit width (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T204-dot-grid-identity-withheld-title/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`) · command 7 (census leg) — T205's census overstated two phases' runtime application (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, finding 3). Merely producing an output does not prove the guard was satisfied — §9's earlier per-command line stands corrected to this form. **Command 8 (census-anchor probes)** — its requirement is a raw probe at a NAMED census instant. T199's A-8 line claimed a probe inside the plate-owned interval [0,800) (its plan-amendment-cycle036.md), and the completion return's finding 1 asks for a CONFIG-derived probe INSIDE that interval; the filed output carries no dump inside it (earliest filed dump at 800 ms). Whether the governing named census instant for that line is a specific instant inside the interval is NOT established on the filed record — **the command-8 assignment is left UNRESOLVED under HQ's deferral** rather than asserted. Independently of the assignment, the A13 receipt defect stands (an index line claiming evidence the filing does not contain). The command's text needs no change; VALIDATION of its filed outputs is part of the HQ deferral in §9b.1.
